archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-04-04T16:17:17Z","updated_at":"2026-04-13T07:53:20Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in master, has been a problem for a while.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev (841c69336) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7700) - AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 63.91 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen word wrap is on, the caret position nominated by clicking past the edge of a wrapped line is on the next line, when it should be the current one. Additionally, when pressing spacebar or backspace on this position, the editing is all happening on the previous line, but the caret remains in place on the next line, giving no feedback to the user.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cf57a8e3-348e-413d-b33e-e2b5a59ec104\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nTurn on word wrap, and type any text that has causes a wrap after a long word, and then start the next line with a long word too.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118195/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118195/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}